{
  "access": "destructive",
  "auth_modes": [
    "api-client",
    "service-account"
  ],
  "body": "Json",
  "description": "The new version takes effect for the users of the app at once: there is no draft and no review. The body describes the whole configuration (configItems and filters as returned by the read operation, with the changes applied); a parameter or condition missing from the body is most likely deleted. version must be the latest version number (0 when the app has no configuration yet): if the configuration was changed after it was read, the request fails with result code 204083201 and nothing is written. The response has the new version number. Rate limit: 5 requests per second and 1000 per hour per IP address.\n\nDestructive: writes a new version of the Remote Configuration from the request body, most likely replacing the whole configuration: it takes effect for the users of the app at once, without a draft or review.\n\nProject-level API client: the server signs this request with the API client of the project given in `productId`, not with its team-level API client. The user adds it with `appgallery-connect-mcp auth project add`.",
  "group": "remoteconfig",
